        {
          "type": "output_text",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": [],
          "text": "{\"occurrence_id\":\"lagerlof-gosta-berlings-saga-baef76cd44bc6283\",\"core_classification\":{\"label_support\":{\"truth_conditional\":4,\"performative\":0,\"exclamatory_reflexive\":0,\"other\":0},\"confidence\":0.95,\"analysis\":\"Marianne’s utterance is principally an avowal that Gösta has always been the exclusive object of her love. Its immediate strategic and possibly self-deceptive use does not diminish its truth-conditional mode. It does not itself undertake a commitment, and the narration portrays it as a deliberate attempt to perform passion rather than an affect-driven verbal discharge.\",\"ambiguity\":\"The sincerity and self-knowledge behind the avowal are unstable: Marianne is consciously trying to win Gösta back and cannot then access a wholehearted feeling, yet the subsequent narration says her love had not been dead and becomes fully conscious only after he leaves. This affects interpretation of truthfulness, not the utterance’s dominant T force.\"},\"other_diagnosis\":{\"tpe_failure\":null,\"core_not_context\":null},\"utterance_status\":{\"status\":\"direct\",\"description\":\"Marianne directly tells Gösta, “jag har aldrig kunnat älska någon annan än dig” (“I have never been able to love anyone but you”), amid pleas that he forgive and not abandon her.\"},\"contextual_interpretation\":\"Marianne says this while deliberately attempting to regain Gösta and to appear passionate; Gösta explicitly rejects it as a lie. The narrator initially emphasizes her cold self-observation and theatrical effort, but after Gösta leaves depicts her love as real though previously suppressed or inaccessible during her weakened condition. The utterance is therefore a strategically deployed and imperfectly self-aware avowal whose underlying content receives retrospective confirmation. Its urgency and surrounding pleas do not independently make it performative or expressive/reflexive.\",\"evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"e1\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"“Gösta, jag har aldrig kunnat älska någon annan än dig” (“Gösta, I have never been able to love anyone but you”).\",\"supports\":\"The grammatical and semantic core directly presents exclusive, enduring love as true, strongly supporting T.\",\"confidence\":0.99},{\"evidence_id\":\"e2\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"Immediately beforehand, the narrator says Marianne “försökte spela passionerad” (“tried to act passionate”) because she did not want to lose him.\",\"supports\":\"The words are produced as a calculated attempt to influence Gösta, which argues against treating their emotional delivery as independent E force.\",\"confidence\":0.99},{\"evidence_id\":\"e3\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"Gösta responds, “Du talar inte sanning ... jag ser, att du ljuger” (“You are not telling the truth ... I can see that you are lying”).\",\"supports\":\"The addressee disputes the avowal’s sincerity or truth, while still treating it as a claim rather than as an undertaking or reflexive discharge.\",\"confidence\":0.98},{\"evidence_id\":\"e4\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"After Gösta leaves, the narrator says Marianne’s love had not been dead; only after her illness had she been unable to feel its power, and she awakened to it too late.\",\"supports\":\"Retrospectively complicates the accusation of lying and suggests latent genuine love, while preserving the utterance’s avowal-like T mode.\",\"confidence\":0.98},{\"evidence_id\":\"e5\",\"source\":\"supplied_metadata\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"The occurrence is identified as an affirmative, perfect-aspect exclusive-target form and reviewed as a valid explicit first-person love expression.\",\"supports\":\"Corroborates identification of the highlighted clause as the core explicit love avowal.\",\"confidence\":0.99}],\"background_knowledge\":{\"used\":false,\"familiarity\":\"none\",\"confidence\":null,\"contribution\":null},\"ontology_assessment\":{\"fit\":\"natural\",\"diagnosis\":\"T naturally represents the core avowal. Its calculation, contested sincerity, and delayed emotional recognition are contextual complexities rather than missing kinds of core force; neither P, E, nor O is needed.\",\"candidate_recurrent_dimension\":null},\"notes\":\"The adjacent imperatives (“Forgive me,” “Do not abandon me”) seek relational continuation, but they are not part of the highlighted love proposition and do not turn that proposition itself into a commitment.\"}"
        }
      ],
